// =====================================================
// Crow's Nest: an e-paper Home Assistant wall panel
// for the Elecrow CrowPanel ESP32-S3 4.2" e-paper display
//
// Board: Elecrow CrowPanel ESP32-S3 4.2" (400 x 300, 1-bit)
// Arduino IDE: ESP32S3 Dev Module, USB CDC On Boot: Disabled,
//   PSRAM: OPI, Partition: Huge APP. Serial monitor 115200.
// Libraries: Arduino_JSON (0.2.x). FreeSans fonts (Adafruit GFX, BSD) are bundled.
//   WiFi / HTTPClient come with the core.
// Elecrow EPD files (EPD*.h/.cpp, EPD_font.h) sit next to this sketch.
// Credentials: secrets.h (copy from secrets.example.h).
// Entities:    config.h (copy from config.example.h): sensors, light
//              tiles (Home Assistant areas), optional mining page.
// Serial log:  the HA template at boot, every request and refresh, and
//              refresh counts (this session and lifetime, kept in NVS).
//
// ---------------- Pages ----------------
//   HOME     outdoor + indoor climate, weather strip, room lights, mining line
//   WEATHER  rain, wind, pressure, UV, sun times
//   MINING   totals, per-miner table, daily/lifetime stats
//
// ---------------- Buttons ----------------
//   MENU           next page (Home, Weather, Mining, then Home again). Fires
//                  on release; held 1 s without the rocker it does nothing.
//   EXIT           go to Home
//   Rocker (Home only; does nothing on other pages):
//     UP / DOWN    move the box between the light tiles (LIGHT_ROOMS)
//     press (OK)   toggle the boxed room (fires on release)
//   hold MENU + UP / DOWN   brighter / dimmer through BRIGHTNESS_LEVELS
//                  (config.h). Only lights already on change; stepping up a
//                  dark room turns it on at the lowest level, stepping below
//                  the lowest turns it off. On an "All" tile every lit light is
//                  set to the same level. The bar right of each bulb shows it.
//   hold OK 1 s     full refresh (clears ghosting) + fresh data
//   hold EXIT 1 s   all lights off ("goodnight"), or all on if all are off
//   hold MENU + EXIT 1 s   Easter egg: a random photo from easter_eggs.h
//                          for EGG_SHOW_MS. Any button returns early;
//                          holding MENU + EXIT again shows another photo.
//
// ---------------- Easter eggs ----------------
//   easter_eggs.h is written by the Image2Eink tool (Image2Eink/README.md),
//   set to the CrowPanel 4.2" preset (400 x 300). Without it the sketch
//   uses the bundled easter_eggs_example.h; with neither, the combo does
//   nothing. Each 400 x 300 photo
//   is 15 KB of flash.
//
// ---------------- Refresh policy (panel wear) ----------------
//   Each frame is rendered to RAM and compared with what is on the panel.
//   Nothing visible changed -> no refresh.
//   "Significant" changes (button input, light states, weather
//   condition, online/offline) -> refresh right away.
//   Number-only changes (temps, hash rate...) -> at most once every
//   MINOR_REFRESH_MIN_MS, and never during quiet hours.
//   Full refresh every AUTO_FULL_EVERY partials, or on MENU hold.
//
// ---------------- Buttons ----------------
//   A FreeRTOS task on core 0 polls the buttons every 5 ms, debounces them
//   and queues press/release events with timestamps. The main loop (core 1)
//   consumes them, so no edge is ever lost while it is busy refreshing the
//   panel or talking to Home Assistant; presses made meanwhile are handled
//   in order right after.
//
// ---------------- Power ----------------
//   Light sleep between polls with WiFi off. RAM is kept, so wake is
//   instant; WiFi reconnects in the background (static IP + cached
//   BSSID/channel keep that short). Any button wakes the chip.
//   After input it stays awake (WiFi up) for AWAKE_AFTER_INPUT_MS so
//   follow-up presses are instant.
// =====================================================

